<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yingchang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yingchang was a city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a> near Dali Lake in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-mongolia">Inner Mongolia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, built by the Khongirad, the consort clan of the Mongol emperors. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toghon-temur">Toghon Temür</a>, the last Yuan emperor, fled there after losing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dadu">Dadu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shangdu">Shangdu</a> to the Ming and died there in 1370, and Ming troops captured it soon afterwards. Its ruins survive.</p></div>
